; Take or carry an object (default handler of the verbs take and carry)
;
; Verb ids $13 (take) and $3B (carry) in VerbHandlers. The subject (Subject)
; takes the first object. Prints "<subject> already carrying <obj1>." when it
; already holds it (#R$9C78). Then #R$8CF1 checks weight and kind. The command
; is refused (#R$9F76) when the first object is something the subject is
; itself in or on: the walk goes up the chain of holders of the subject
; looking for the first object. When the command is really performed
; (#R$9D44) the first object's holder (+1) becomes the subject. If its holder
; was the rope (OBJ_ROPE; apparently the object is tied to it), the rope's
; own holder ($C367) is set instead, so the rope comes with the subject.
; .
; Hardware: none.
@label=VerbTake
c$8D33 CALL $9C78    ; already held?
 $8D36 LD HL,$AE11   ; "{SUBJ_IS} already carrying {OBJ1}."
 $8D39 JP C,$72DD    ;
*$8D3C CALL $8CF1    ; can the subject lift and carry it?
 $8D3F LD A,($B6EA)  ; the subject
@label=VerbTake_Up
*$8D42 CALL $9BCA    ; record of A
 $8D45 LD A,($B6E8)  ;
 $8D48 CP (IX+$01)   ; is the first object this one's holder?
 $8D4B JP Z,$9F76    ; yes: refuse
 $8D4E LD A,(IX+$01) ; go up to the holder
@isub=CP AT_LOCATION
 $8D51 CP $FF        ;
 $8D53 JR NZ,$8D42   ;
 $8D55 LD IX,($B708) ; the first object
 $8D59 CALL $9D44    ; only when really performing
 $8D5C LD A,(IX+$01) ;
@isub=CP OBJ_ROPE
 $8D5F CP $12        ; tied to the rope?
 $8D61 LD A,($B6EA)  ; the subject
 $8D64 JR Z,$8D6A    ;
 $8D66 LD (IX+$01),A ; the object is now held by the subject
 $8D69 RET           ;
@isub=LD (Obj12Rope+1),A
*$8D6A LD ($C367),A  ; the rope is held by the subject (holder field of the rope record $C366)
 $8D6D RET           ;
